    A region is recolored TEAL iff:
      (a) single lobe forming a square-bbox diagonal staircase (bbox NxN, N>=4,
          fill <=50%, occupies opposite corners NW+SE or NE+SW), OR
      (b) multi-lobe: every lobe pair shares at most 1 diagonal contact direction,
          lobes form a non-branching chain (max degree <=2), AND the region is
          NOT: all singletons not on one diagonal line, all lobes on same border
          side, or a 2-lobe (1-cell + >=5-cell) where not all lobes touch border.
  target_region_stats:
    size: 3-11 pixels
    lobes: 1-4
    diagonal_run: >=3 pixels
  distractor_categories: |
    - Single-lobe non-staircase blobs/bars/rectangles (most common)
    - Isolated single pixels (size 1)
    - Multi-lobe with branching (degree>2)
    - Multi-lobe with multi-direction diagonal contact between a pair
    - Multi-lobe chain but all lobes on same grid border
    - All-singleton chain not along a single diagonal
    - 2-lobe (singleton + large) where not both lobes touch grid border

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct placement with classification guarantee
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size H x W in observed ranges.
    2. Build 1-3 target regions (to be recolored):
       - For staircase type, draw a square NxN (N=4-6) diagonal staircase
         spanning opposite corners of its bbox; require a straight diagonal
         run of length >=3.
       - For chain type, grow 2-4 lobes connected by single diagonal contacts
         in a non-branching chain; require a straight diagonal run of length
         >=3 and ensure none of the rejection rules apply.
    3. Build 3-15 distractor regions from varied categories:
       - Compact 4-connected blobs (rectangles, L-shapes, bars) -- most common.
       - Isolated single pixels scattered around.
       - Optionally 1-2 near-miss distractors (chain with branching, or
         multi-direction contact, or same-border-side chain) for difficulty.
    4. Place all regions on the ORANGE grid ensuring 8-connected separation
       between distinct regions (no two regions share an 8-neighbor).
    5. Verify GREY density is 30-40%; adjust region count/sizes if needed.

